  "profile": {
    "video_id": "kenji:021KahIfXfA",
    "purpose": "A livestreamed Patreon Q&A in which Kenji, with producers Lena and Erin, answers community questions. Topics include cutting boards, cooktops, woks, stock, carryover cooking, stew texture, knife sharpening, his weekly cooking routine and kids, Seattle, gardening, restaurant high-heat cooking, kitchen smoke, and an upcoming halal cart chicken update.",
    "video_type": "other",
    "thesis": "A wide-ranging 'Ask Kenji Anything' session covering practical questions on kitchen tools, woks, cooking technique and home life. It is organised as a series of chat questions, each answered in turn.",
    "key_takeaways": [
      "Covers wooden cutting boards: why Kenji uses them, how to clean, oil and resurface them, and why to avoid metal, glass and titanium boards.",
      "Compares induction and gas cooktops, including the limits of induction for wok cooking and using a portable butane burner as a workaround.",
      "Explains how to clean a wok, and how wok seasoning differs from cast-iron seasoning.",
      "Gives advice for beginners intimidated by wok cooking, including cheaper starter woks versus his new nitrided wok.",
      "Discusses using pork trotters in stock: raw versus roasted bones, and getting the most gelatin out.",
      "Explains the variables behind carryover cooking and practical ways to deal with them.",
      "Describes the stages of meat breakdown in braises for diagnosing tough versus overcooked stew meat, plus umami substitutes for Marmite.",
      "Covers knife sharpening options for regular people, and the difference between honing and sharpening.",
      "Personal segments on his weekly cooking routine, picky kids, seafood, Seattle recommendations, pearl onions and gardening.",
      "Discusses high-heat restaurant cooking, managing smoke in small kitchens, and an update on the halal cart chicken and rice recipe."
    ],
